The TypeScript adaptation keeps the double arithmetic of the plain C formula
in native order (no fused multiply-add), as the Linux x86-64 reference
evaluates it, using only +, -, *, /, fabs and fmod. It refuses mode=sine (the
default, which needs libm sin()), timeline enable, runtime commands, option
expressions, fractional values for integer options, non-stereo or masked
layouts that native would convert implicitly, non-finite input samples and NaN
output, instead of approximating them. It adds no FFmpeg runtime code. The
original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
